{"text": "Halvorsen Pruitt & Achebe LLP\nAttorneys at Law\n600 Grant Street, 41st Floor\nPittsburgh, Pennsylvania 15219-2702\nTel. 412-555-0118 / Fax 412-555-0119\nJanuary 22, 2026\nVIA EMAIL (ngozi.okafor@okafortrust.example) AND FIRST-CLASS MAIL\nMs. Ngozi A. Okafor, Trustee\nThe Okafor Family Trust\nP.O. Box 8842\nSewickley, PA 15143\nRe: Engagement for representation; Okafor Family Trust adv. Emeka Okafor; our matter no. 20260114.0003\nDear Ms. Okafor:\nThank you for selecting Halvorsen Pruitt & Achebe LLP (the \"Firm\") to represent you in your capacity as successor trustee of the Okafor Family Trust, u/a/d April 9, 2003 (the \"Trust\"), in connection with the petition filed by your brother, Emeka Okafor, in the Orphans' Court Division of the Court of Common Pleas of Allegheny County at No. 02-25-06617. This letter and the enclosed Standard Terms describe the basis on which we will provide legal services. Please read both carefully.\n1. Scope. We will represent you, as trustee only, in defending the petition for an accounting and for your removal, and in the related dispute over the proposed sale of the late Dr. Chukwuma Okafor's former medical office at 1187 Beaver Street in Sewickley (the \"Beaver Street property\"). We do not represent you individually, the Trust's other beneficiaries, or Okafor Pediatrics, P.C. Tax advice and preparation of the Trust's Form 1041 remain with your accountants at Brindle & Vasquez CPAs. If you later ask us to take on additional work, we will confirm that in writing.\n2. Staffing and rates. I will have primary responsibility for the matter. My 2026 rate is $525 per hour. Thomas J. Achebe (associate, $340 per hour) and paralegal Wendy Pruitt-Sato ($185 per hour) will assist where that is more economical. Rates are adjusted each January. We bill in tenths of an hour and send statements monthly.\n3. Retainer. We ask for an advance of $7,500, which will be held in our IOLTA account and applied to our final invoice. You may pay by check or by wire to Three Rivers Bank & Trust, ABA 102560066, account no. 4000 7731 8852, reference 20260114.0003. You may also pay online at https://pay.hpa-law.example/retainer. Under Rule 1.15 we must keep these funds separate from the Firm's own money until they are earned.\n4. Conflicts. As we discussed on January 14, the Firm represented Sewickley Valley Savings Bank (\"SVSB\"), the Trust's lender, in unrelated matters that concluded in 2022. We do not believe this creates a conflict, and you have agreed to waive any conflict that may exist. SVSB has given its consent as well.\n5. Communication. You have asked that we not call your office line. We will use your mobile, (412) 555-0171, and the email address above. Documents will be shared through our client portal; your username is nokafor-trustee and a temporary password will be sent to you separately.\n6. Document retention. We keep closed files for seven years and then destroy them unless you ask us in writing to return them.\nIf these terms are acceptable, please sign below and return a copy with the retainer by February 6, 2026. You may end our engagement at any time.\nVery truly yours,\nIngrid M. Halvorsen\nPA Attorney ID No. 87214\nimh@hpa-law.example / direct 412.555.0122\ncc: T. Achebe\nACKNOWLEDGED AND AGREED:\n______________________ NGOZI A. OKAFOR, as Trustee and not individually. Date: __________", "kind": "Word document", "detail": "545 words", "notes": [], "names": {"people": ["Ingrid M. Halvorsen", "Emeka Okafor", "Wendy Pruitt-Sato"], "companies": ["Halvorsen Pruitt & Achebe LLP", "Three Rivers Bank & Trust", "Sewickley Valley Savings Bank", "Brindle & Vasquez CPAs", "Okafor Pediatrics, P.C.", "okafortrust.example", "hpa-law.example", "example"]}, "topics": {"places": ["Pittsburgh", "Sewickley", "Allegheny County", "Sewickley Valley Savings Bank"], "health": [], "sensitive": ["Trustee", "Successor trustee"], "names": ["Halvorsen", "Pruitt", "Achebe", "Emeka", "Ngozi"]}, "chunks": 1, "chunkErrors